2,A Theoretically and Comparatively Informed Description of Yogad Morphology,https://carleton.scholaris.ca/bitstreams/6d99ef72-08d8-41e1-b248-b7e229b3e343/download,"Abstract Yogad is an Austronesian language spoken in the Northern Philippines by approximately 16,000 speakers. Previous descriptive work on Yogad follows a nonaprioristic approach, where no categories are imported from other languages. This description makes it difficult to gloss functional morphemes or to discuss Yogad in a cross-linguistic ...",Yogad,Austronesian
3,ABOUT YOGAD - Yogad Kan,http://www.yogadkan.com/about-yogad.html,"Ethnologue (Simons et al., 2017) classifies Yogad as Malayo-Polynesian, belonging to the Austronesian language family. Locally, it is categorized under the Ibanagic group of the Northern Cordilleran languages found in the Cagayan Valley, which also includes Gaddang, Itawit, Villaviciosa Agta, Ibanag, Atta, and Isnag.",Yogad,Austronesian
4,Yogad Folk Songs of Echague: Reflections of Life and of Love,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/352897737_Yogad_Folk_Songs_of_Echague_Reflections_of_Life_and_of_Love,"This paper endeavors to retrieve and translate a collection of Yogad folk songs of Echague, Isabela, Philippines. It further explores the folk songs thematically to establish the Yogad's identity ...",Yogad,Austronesian
5,Yogad Folksongs of Echague: Reflections of Life and of Love,https://submit.iafor.org/paper/submission21867/,"This paper endeavored to translate a collection of Yogad folk songs of Echague, Isabela, Philippines. It further explores the folk songs thematically to establish the Yogad's identity as indigenous peoples. The paper establishes the significant role of folk songs in the life cycle of the Yogad tribe reflecting their culture and traditions.",Yogad,Austronesian
6,Austronesian Music - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLnOSH5j1sQh9pFS_rqvm3r2JtCD8AGOa-,"Austronesian culture includes more than 1200 ethnic groups, across South Asia, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, the Philippines, parts of China, as well as the Pacific as far afield as the Maori in New ...",Yogad,Austronesian
